cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If AgentSynth is part of your research, please cite it as below.
title: "AgentSynth: outcome-verified benchmarks and synthetic trajectories for LLM agents"
type: software
authors:
  - name: AgentSynth contributors
repository-code: https://github.com/agentsynth/agentsynth
url: https://agentsynth.tech
license: MIT
version: 0.9.0
date-released: "2026-06-23"
abstract: >-
  AgentSynth generates synthetic multi-turn agent trajectories and verifies them
  against the world's end state rather than the transcript. Scenario packs double
  as benchmarks with reward-hacking audits, contamination canaries, pass^k
  reliability, and reproducible run manifests, and export to the verifiers and
  OpenEnv ecosystems for RL training.
keywords:
  - llm-agents
  - benchmark
  - evaluation
  - reinforcement-learning
  - verifiable-rewards
  - synthetic-data
  - reproducibility
